(www.freetype.org). All rights reserved.

The shaper of stxlib::glyphs (include/stxlib/glyph_shape.hpp and
glyph_shape.cpp, layout_tables, shape_buffer, shape_digest, shape_unicode,
shape_plan, shape_apply and shape_text in this folder) is a conversion to
house-style C++ of harfrust, a port to Rust of HarfBuzz:

- harfrust 0.16.0 (https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfrust), taken under the
  MIT licence: the buffer, the reading of the layout tables, the plan and
  its map of features, the applying of substitution and positioning
  lookups, normalisation, the default, Hebrew and Hangul shapers and the
  fallbacks. Its notice is below.
- HarfBuzz 14.6.0 (https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz), which harfrust
  follows and whose results the shaper is measured against. Where the two
  differ in how a number is rounded or scaled, HarfBuzz's rule was taken,
  read from its source (how a real number is rounded, the widths of
  fallback spaces, the gap of a mark placed without the font's help, an
  advance taken from a FreeType font). HarfBuzz's notice ("Old MIT") is
  below. None of HarfBuzz's or harfrust's files is in this tree, and
  neither is compiled or linked.

shape_unicode.inc holds values of the Unicode Character Database 18.0 as
harfrust 0.16.0 has them in its own generated tables (general category,
script, combining class, mirroring, canonical decomposition and
composition, Extended_Pictographic), written by tools/gen_shape_unicode.py.
The Unicode data is under the Unicode License v3, whose notice is in
third_party/unicode-18.0.0/LICENSE.

The rasterizer of stxlib::glyphs (glyph_mask.hpp, mask.cpp, chords.hpp,
flatten.hpp, centres.hpp, reciprocal.hpp), its glyph store
(glyph_store.hpp, glyph_store.cpp) and its face (glyph_face.hpp,
glyph_face.cpp) are not a conversion of any of these.

